  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner who became paralysed after a riding accident in 2007, has died at age 44 following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. She was known for completing a marathon in a bionic suit and raising nearly £1 million for charity. Lomas gained recognition for running the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days wearing the suit and lighting the Paralympic cauldron later that year. She also participated in the Great North Run in 2016 while pregnant, completing it in five days with the bionic suit."
